  "label": "User projected onto the juxtaposed religious scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the juxtaposed religious scene (juxtaposed_religious_scene) where a man is carrying a cross while being escorted by police. This scene is contrasted with the text 'some people say religion is a labor of love,' implying the user is being invited to view religious devotion through the lens of coercion or burden, rather than voluntary sacrifice. The projection is implicit, as the meme does not use explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me,' but the user is expected to identify with the critical perspective presented by the juxtaposition.",
